  "problem": "Source-native release and distribution identities were not bound. Rolling endpoints, replacement files, one-to-many distributions and conflicting date roles could be collapsed, and human manifest hashes did not map to machine generation labels.",
  "resulting_behavior": "PR-007 reuses existing identity and registry contracts to mint release/distribution IDs from publisher identifiers, locators, typed date roles and hash-scoped content when no stable release ID exists. Captured catalog/resources records bind deterministically with evidence pointers; ambiguous URLs and rolling resources never fabricate exact releases. One explicit human-manifest/machine-generation/dictionary-source-revision map returns the same product context, and stale or mismatched pins yield typed restart guidance. Existing observatory asset IDs are unchanged. Dictionary applicability remains unresolved and is not scientific approval. Execution.provider grok, dispatch model grok-4; this interface is Grok 4.6 and is not a serving-model attestation.",
